{"slug":"street-racing-syndicate","title":"Street Racing Syndicate","desc":"PC, Eutechnyx / Namco 2004-2005","notes":["Read from CDFILES.DAT + archive.ar with technyx.py.  The 51 cars of the game (with the trim levels that have files of their own), folder names are the game's file codes.","A car is its stock set UPG0: body with windows, cabin and engine, bonnet, boot lid, bumpers, exhaust, spoiler, and 4 wheels on the DummyWheel nodes of the body file (rim, brake disc and caliper, the caliper turned by the CALIPER-ANGLE of the vehicle script).  The pop-up lamps of the RX-7 and the Trueno are raised in the files, cabins are mostly black.","TYRES: there are no tyre models in the game.  It builds them at run time from the TYREGEN blocks of its script (size, a 3 point profile, a tread and a side picture).  The tyres here are built the same way, with the size that the vehicle script gives each axle and the game's own pictures.","KITS: every upgrade of the shop (body kits, bonnets, boot lids, bumpers, spoilers, exhausts) is in the hidden 'Variants' folder of <car>.fbx and, to be seen, in <car>_kits.fbx: the stock car and one complete car per upgrade number, all VISIBLE, in rows of 6.","Paint: the painted panels are palette pictures, the game replaces the first entries of the palette (the grey ramp of the paint).  Here those entries are multiplied by one red.","Left out: stickers (blank decal cards), damage overlays, light glows and sprites, the brake upgrades, the lower levels of detail (_X files) and the driver.","RIMS: the folder _Rims holds the 24 rims of the shop and the 30 different stock rims, one rim per folder, in the size of the file, standing on the ground, outer face towards +X.","Each shop rim exists once per car in the game; _aliases.csv lists the copies (same pictures, same number of vertices).","TRAFFIC: the folder _Traffic holds the 15 vehicles that are one file each, wheels and tyres included, in the game's own colours, highest level of detail: the traffic cars (CAR1, CAR2 = taxi, TRUCK), the police (POLICECAR, POLICEVAN) and the tuned cars of the rival crews with their liveries (LSCAR, NXCAR, SRCAR, TNCAR, VFCAR, VRCAR).","VINYLS: the folder _Vinyls/<car> holds the 20 vinyls of the car as PNG with transparency, one picture per painted panel (V05_body, V05_bonnet, V05_trunk; upg1 = for body kit 1).","V05_body.png is the whole design: the grey areas take a second colour in the game and are one flat grey here, recolour them at will.  V05_body_art.png is only the art on it (the coloured and white parts), when there is any.  The cars keep the vinyl in the picture of the panel: door lines and body shading were taken out with the picture of the same panel without vinyl (V0), the wheel arches are transparent.  The pictures are the size of the game's, 512 x 128 for the side of a car.  _sheet.jpg shows the side vinyls of a car."],"tags":["street-racing-syndicate"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["350Z","",9853182,"street-racing-syndicate","car-350Z.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-350Z.webp"],["350Z_ENTH","",9843126,"street-racing-syndicate","car-350Z_ENTH.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-350Z_ENTH.webp"],["350Z_PERF","",9712753,"street-racing-syndicate","car-350Z_PERF.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-350Z_PERF.webp"],["350Z_TOUR","",9712778,"street-racing-syndicate","car-350Z_TOUR.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-350Z_TOUR.webp"],["350Z_TRACK","",10637671,"street-racing-syndicate","car-350Z_TRACK.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-350Z_TRACK.webp"],["CELICA00GT","",9143230,"street-racing-syndicate","car-CELICA00GT.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-CELICA00GT.webp"],["CELICA00GTS","",9694150,"street-racing-syndicate","car-CELICA00GTS.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-CELICA00GTS.webp"],["CELICA04GT","",9102686,"street-racing-syndicate","car-CELICA04GT.zip","thumbs/street-racing-syndicate/cars/car-CELICA04GT.webp"],["CELI